    "result_text": "Compiles cleanly and the full suite is green (70/70). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. The change spans four areas, exactly as specified:\n\n**1. Identity derivation \u2014 rederived with a fixed `V2` tag (region code inside the identifiers)**\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.generateMemberId` now builds the member id from a **versioned region** (`\"V2\" + regionFor(owner)`, e.g. `V2NSW\u2026`) instead of the plain region.\n- `OwnerMapper.householdId` and `OwnerMapper.identityKey` now mix the `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG` (`\"V2\"`) into their SHA-256 inputs.\n- Result: every memberId, householdId and identityKey changes, and no value produced under v1 can recur. `identityKey` stays a 64-char lowercase SHA-256 (Cp28).\n\n**2. `locality`/`timezone`/owner-segment region stay plain (no V2 leak)**\n- Previously `locality` was parsed out of the memberId \u2014 which would now yield the V2-tagged region. I **decoupled** it: added a plain `region(owner)` derivation (postcode-first, city fallback) in `OwnerMapper`, and `locality`, `timezone` and `ownerSegment` all use it. So `locality` remains `\"NSW\"` (Cp17/Cp30/Cp42) and `ownerSegment` remains `STANDARD_METRO` (Cp55), recomputed from the v2 identity path.\n\n**3. Response shape \u2014 nested `identity` + top-level `apiVersion`**\n- Added an `OwnerIdentity` schema to `openapi.yml`, moved `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId` under a nested `identity` object, removed them from the top level, and added a top-level integer `apiVersion` (2). The mapper builds the `identity` object and sets `apiVersion` via `apiVersion()`.\n\n**4. Audit schema v2**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent.toJson()` now emits `\"schemaVersion\":2`, still carrying the owner id and the (now v2) memberId (Cp53).\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. Full offline test run: **70 passed, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS.**",
