    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, as the code currently stands. There are two phases: framework bean-validation (before the controller body runs), then the imperative logic inside `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Security & framework bean-validation (before the method body)\n1. **`@PreAuthorize` role check** \u2014 caller must have role `OWNER_ADMIN`, else 403.\n2. **Jakarta Bean Validation** on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (failure \u2192 400 `MethodArgumentNotValidException`):\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max = 10)`\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max = 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[-0-9 ()+.]*$)`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max = 255)`, `@Email`\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Controller body (`addOwner`), in exact order\n3. **Idempotency replay** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header matches a prior create, return the existing owner with **200** (short-circuit, no side-effects).\n4. **`applyAddressFields`** *(side-effect: mutates input)* \u2014 trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE), and composes flat `address` from `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`.\n5. **`validateRequiredFields`** \u2014 firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone must be non-blank \u2192 else 400.\n6. **`validatePostcode`** \u2014 if present, must be 4 digits **and** fall in the city's regional range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else 400.\n7. **`normalizeTelephone`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 strips separators, assumes +61 when no `+`, drops leading 0, requires `+` then 8\u201315 digits with correct national length (AU=9, NANP=10) \u2192 else 400.\n8. **`requireCityHasCapacity`** \u2014 hard cap: \u226550 owners in the city \u2192 409.\n9. **`normalizeEmail`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 blank\u2192null; else must match email pattern, is lower-cased, and disposable domains (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) are rejected \u2192 400.\n10. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`; id and pets ignored).\n11. *(side-effect)* set normalized `telephone`, normalized `email`, and `deleted = false`.\n12. **`requireUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 computes an identity key and scans all non-deleted owners; collision \u2192 409.\n13. Read `sharesHousehold` flag.\n14. **`requireRegistrationDateNotInFuture`** \u2014 registrationDate must not be in the future \u2192 400.\n15. *(side-effect \u2014 defaulting)* **registrationDate defaulting**: if absent \u2192 today; then **`toBusinessDay`** rolls weekends/2026 public holidays forward; result stored on the owner.\n16. **`requireDailyLimitNotReached`** \u2014 hard cap: \u2265100 owners created for that date \u2192 **429**.\n17. *(side-effect \u2014 flags)* set **`bulkSignupWarning`** (>80 same-day), **`capacityWarning`** (40\u201349 owners in city).\n18. *(side-effect \u2014 flags)* **duplicate detection**: unless `sharesHousehold`, soft-match on Soundex(lastName)+postcode; set `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n19. *(side-effect)* set **`membershipLevelCap`** = max existing household member level + 1.\n20. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 persists in its own transaction; on new owners assigns *(side-effects)* **`memberId`** (region+FY+SHA-256 hash+Luhn check, de-duplicated), **`namesakeCount`**, and **`householdMemberCount`**, then `repository.save` (INSERT).\n21. *(side-effect)* record the `Idempotency-Key` \u2192 new owner id, if a key was supplied.\n22. *(side-effects \u2014 logging only)* two `AUDIT` log lines (`owner created \u2026` and a structured `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event) and one `NOTIFY` \"welcome owner\" line. **No real email or Spring event is published \u2014 these are log emissions.**\n23. *(side-effect)* set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and return **201 Created** with the mapped `OwnerDto`.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- **No `@Transactional` on `addOwner`** \u2014 each service/validation call is its own transaction, so the capacity/daily-limit/uniqueness reads and the final save are **not atomic** (a race can exceed caps or create duplicates).\n- **No JPA lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist`/`@EntityListeners`) and **no `ApplicationEventPublisher`/`@EventListener`** anywhere \u2014 all \"events\" are logger output.\n- The entity `Owner`/`Person` also carry `@NotEmpty` (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone) and `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)` on telephone, but these are **not actively enforced** on this path (validation is driven by the DTO, and the service doesn't re-validate the entity).\n- Several duplicate-exception handlers (telephone/email/household) exist in the advice but are **not triggered** by the current create logic \u2014 dedup is consolidated into `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`.\n\nNothing was modified."
